sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-flying-fish-segmentation-favours-kcnh2a-not-kcnk5b> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "The one flying-fish trait that can be compared with the two zebrafish fin-overgrowth mutants argues against kcnk5b as the flying-fish mechanism: flying fishes and the longfin (kcnh2a) mutant keep regular fin-ray segmentation, whereas the kcnk5b mutant has irregular segmentation" ;
    dct:description "Status: supported, at the weakest useful grade (association): a morphological comparison, not a manipulation in a flying fish. Daane 2021 states that \"lof mutants maintain elongate but regular segmented lepidotrichia (Figures S2A and S2B), in contrast to the kcnk5balf fin overgrowth mutant having irregular segmentation\". Perathoner 2014 independently describes the kcnk5b allele as having, on average, increased segment length with \"structures appearing as very short segments\" occasionally present, and an unchanged segment number. Since flying-fish fins are elongated with regular segmentation, the kcnh2a-like mechanism matches the flying-fish fin and the kcnk5b-like mechanism does not. This is the only point in this project where a flying-fish observation discriminates between two candidate mechanisms, and it discriminates against the better-supported one. What it does not establish: It does not establish that kcnh2a is the flying-fish mechanism: the flying-fish evidence for that locus is comparative-genomic only, and the sufficiency experiment behind it used human KCNH2, not zebrafish kcnh2a. It does not exclude kcnk5b from contributing, and segmentation regularity was not quantified in flying fishes by this thread or, as far as the fetched sources show, by anyone. Pre-registration: none: a comparison noticed while grading the chains. It was recorded because it tells against the project's own best-supported chain, which is the kind of result a thread is most tempted to leave out." ;
    delphi:context "Graded association in genotype/causal-chains.json (cross_gene). The comparison is between published descriptions of fin-ray segmentation, not a measurement made by this thread. The two zebrafish mutants are kcnk5b (alf, gain of function) and the longfin regulatory allele that overexpresses kcnh2a." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-flying-fish-segmentation-favours-kcnh2a-not-kcnk5b> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-genotype-thread-claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-flying-fish-segmentation-favours-kcnh2a-not-kcnk5b> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Published descriptions of fin-ray segmentation in kcnk5b and kcnh2a mutants and in flying fishes" ;
    dct:description "Read from genotype/causal-chains.json, cross_gene claims, with verbatim quotes from the two papers." ;
    delphi:statisticalTest "Comparison of published morphological descriptions of lepidotrichial segmentation in two zebrafish fin-overgrowth mutants and in flying fishes. No statistical test; no measurement by this thread." ;
    dct:source <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24453984/>, <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34534441/> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom sub:chains ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/genotype/data.json> .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24453984/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Bioelectric signaling regulates size in zebrafish fins." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Perathoner S 2014 PLoS Genet" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 24453984" , "doi:10.1371/journal.pgen.1004080" ;
    delphi:context "full text read" ;
    rdfs:comment "Here, we show that alf mutants carry gain-of-function mutations in kcnk5b, a gene encoding a two-pore domain potassium (K+) channel." .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34534441/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Modulation of bioelectric cues in the evolution of flying fishes." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Daane JM 2021 Curr Biol" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 34534441" , "doi:10.1016/j.cub.2021.08.054" ;
    delphi:context "full text read" ;
    rdfs:comment "Thus, the chromosomal rearrangement in lof changes the regulation of the potassium channel kcnh2a, enhancing kcnh2a expression in the forming fin and is sufficient for increased fin size." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-flying-fish-segmentation-favours-kcnh2a-not-kcnk5b> schema:additionalProperty sub:m0 .
  sub:m0 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "status" ; schema:value "supported, at the weakest useful grade (association): a morphological comparison, not a manipulation in a flying fish" ; schema:description "status of this record in the words of AGENTS.md (supported, refuted, mixed, inconclusive, or a descriptive status)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-flying-fish-segmentation-favours-kcnh2a-not-kcnk5b> schema:additionalProperty sub:m1 .
  sub:m1 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "candidate_mechanisms_compared" ; schema:value "2"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "kcnk5b and kcnh2a" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-flying-fish-segmentation-favours-kcnh2a-not-kcnk5b> schema:additionalProperty sub:m2 .
  sub:m2 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "discriminating_traits_found" ; schema:value "1"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "regularity of lepidotrichial segmentation" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-flying-fish-segmentation-favours-kcnh2a-not-kcnk5b> schema:additionalProperty sub:m3 .
  sub:m3 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "flying_fish_manipulations" ; schema:value "0"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "experiments in any flying fish supporting either mechanism" .
  sub:map a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "genotype/map.vetted.json (vetted, slimmed genotype-phenotype map; built 2026-10-31T18:58:34Z by genotype/build.py)" ;
    spdx:checksum sub:map-sha ;
    schema:contentSize "9197138"^^xsd:integer ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-31T18:58:34Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
  sub:map-sha a spdx:Checksum ; spdx:algorithm spdx:checksumAlgorithm_sha256 ; spdx:checksumValue "c177dafdfc606e821ee55e6b8ac77ee10256fde7280f2df8963f6347b3223ff2" .
  sub:chains a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "genotype/causal-chains.json (causal chains with a source and an evidence grade on every link; built 2026-10-31T20:48:28Z)" ;
    spdx:checksum sub:chains-sha ;
    schema:contentSize "368282"^^xsd:integer ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-31T20:48:28Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:comment "Every link was produced by a subagent working under genotype/AGENT_BRIEF.md: nothing from memory, every statement from a document fetched in that run through the logged fetcher, a verbatim quote per source, and an evidence grade of association (expression only), necessity (loss of function), sufficiency (gain of function), mechanism (a pathway step shown experimentally) or hypothesis (proposed, not shown). A grade is about the link it sits on, not the gene. All of it is zebrafish or other proxy-species work: no flying-fish experiment exists. This file was merged and checked by genotype/assemble_chains.py, which upgrades nothing; validation flags travel with the data." .
  sub:chains-sha a spdx:Checksum ; spdx:algorithm spdx:checksumAlgorithm_sha256 ; spdx:checksumValue "bdc69e233fce91e6cade3cc8fc6eb5b60039a3ab4135ac7ab4a82069a749eebf" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-genotype-thread-claude-fable-5-1> a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "delphisci genotype thread (session scienceclaw-68, Claude Fable 5.1): built and vetted the genotype-phenotype map from proxy-fish records" ;
    delphi:usesModel <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a delphi:LanguageModel ; rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1" ; dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" .
